{
  "dom_id": "step-29583",
  "name": "The Image of a Line Under a Dilation",
  "problem": "If $l$ is a line passing through the center of dilation, then the image $l'$ under the dilation is the same as the original line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/eb208ea1b492a1d471e0ffb6b3f23fa80a4747f3b5f6da1ad126c30716e52743.png)\n\nHowever, if $k$ is a line that does not pass through the center of dilation, then the image $k'$ is parallel to the original line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/09a11211bde36f85dfe48e4a769314d084edc99c523b869ed3f9a518784fb9a6.png)",
